-- Section 1: Static Batching --

  Static batching runs a fixed batch to completion: every slot is occupied
  until the LONGEST sequence in the batch finishes, wasting the freed slots.

  Requests        : 8  | slots: 4
  Total steps     : 110
  Slot utilization:  51.4%  (useful tokens / slot-steps held)

-- Section 2: Continuous Batching --

  Continuous batching evicts a finished sequence the moment it emits its last
  token and admits a waiting request into that slot the next step.

  Total steps     : 62
  Slot utilization:  91.1%
  Step speedup vs static: 1.77x
  [check] continuous batching finishes sooner with higher slot utilization

-- Section 3: PagedAttention Block Allocation --

  Each sequence's KV cache is stored in fixed-size blocks, allocated lazily as
  the sequence grows - no up-front reservation of max_seq_len.

  Block size            : 16 tokens
  Blocks after prefill  : 3
  Blocks at completion  : 7
  Naive pre-reservation : 128 blocks (max_seq_len=2048)
  Memory saved vs naive :  94.5%
  [check] lazy paged allocation avoids reserving the worst-case context

